= The Stowford Front

The <span style="color: #7A3C00;">far</span>-<span style="color: #003755;">right</span> parties and paramilitaries - the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> (and its paramilitary the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span>), the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Wardens**</span> paramilitary group, and the <span style="color: #003755;">**DNF**</span> - have united to form the Stowford Front, as a force dedicated to the overthrow of the current government. 

However, this show of unity lacks substance, as Mallin, Gallax, and the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Wardens**</span> compete against one another to assert themselves as the leader of the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">national</span> <span style="color: #003755;">opposition</span>. Gallax's erratic behavior—such as vanishing from the podium when <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Wardens**</span> detachments march by—has offended many conservatives[? if bruning_time:, and inter-party polemics may only serve to reinforce Askew against their pressures?]. Luckily, the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>'s leadership has dissuaded many influential guild-masters from taking part in this gathering. However, the inclusion of the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Wardens**</span> in this alliance—and a quiet, growing nostalgia for the old Empire—pressures the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> to move toward closer ties.

